Package: noisecanceling
Type: Package
Title: Correcting Questionnaires for Acquiescence Response Bias
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Ricardo",
           family = "Primi",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "rprimi@mac.com")
Description: Tools for measuring and correcting acquiescence response bias
    (the tendency to agree with items regardless of their content) in
    psychological questionnaires built with balanced scales. Balanced scales
    pair positively keyed (PK) and negatively keyed (NK) items so that a
    per-person acquiescence index can be estimated and removed by centering
    item responses. The approach works like noise-cancelling headphones: the
    trait is the signal, acquiescence is the noise, and inverting the negatively
    keyed items aligns the signal so that the noise cancels out. The package
    implements the classical centering correction together with helpers for
    scoring, classical psychometric analysis, and reporting.
